<title>USA: Ill. utility wins round in tax assessment fight.</title>
<headline>Ill. utility wins round in tax assessment fight.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Illinois Appellate Court has upheld lower property assessments for an Illinois electric utility's nuclear plant in Byron, the Chicago Tribune reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the move could cut Commonwealth Edison Co.'s $40.1 million annual tax bill by $27 million.</p>
<p>The appeal was filed by a group of local governments in Ogle County after the Illinois Property Tax Appeal Board approved a retroactive lowering of the nuclear plant's tax bill.</p>
<p>An attorney representing the governments has said that refunds owed the utitility would be financially devastating for the governments.</p>
<p>   --Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647</p>
